    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_title">Keep xDrip+ running</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_intro">On some phones, you can lock xDrip+ in Recents so that clearing recent apps does not remove it.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_step_1">1. Open recent apps using the square navigation button. If you use gestures, swipe up from the bottom and hold briefly.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_step_2">2. Find the xDrip+ preview among your recent apps.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_step_3">3. Touch and hold the xDrip+ preview to open its options.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_step_4">4. Tap the padlock or pin icon if it protects the app from being cleared.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_step_5">5. Do not swipe the xDrip+ preview away. To clear other apps, use the general X-shaped clear button if available.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_note">Menus and gestures vary by phone. Some devices do not offer this feature. This is not Android screen pinning, and xDrip+ cannot automatically verify the lock.</string>
    <string name="source_wizard_app_lock_help_close">Got it</string>
